  "result": "I found and fixed two bugs in `src/`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests. I didn't touch the tests.\n\n1. **`src/cart.js`: discount and tax were applied in the wrong order.** `total()` added tax first and then took the discount off the taxed amount. The code's own comment says the discount should come off the pre-tax subtotal, so I swapped the order: discount first, then tax on what's left. Percent discounts gave the same answer either way, which is why only the fixed-discount test failed (got 90, expected 88).\n2. **`src/discount.js`: a fixed discount could push the total below zero.** A fixed discount bigger than the subtotal gave a negative total (-14.5). It now stops at zero with `Math.max(0, amount - discount.value)`, as the comment in `cart.js` says it should.",
